IMPORT prelude
IMPORT `cur-tender`

-- Currency Act 1967, ss 11-14, 18-20, 23, 25, 26 -- worked cases.
--
-- Every assertion is a claim about the ENCODING on stated facts, not about the law. Nothing here has been checked
-- against a decided case or subsidiary legislation (none was retrieved).
--
-- Fixtures are generated from a table of which flags are set (scratchpad gen_currency-act-1967.py). Expected results were written by
-- hand from the text.

`a 50-dollar note for a 500-dollar bill` MEANS Tender WITH
    `is a coin` IS FALSE
    `face value in cents` IS 5000
    `payment due in cents` IS 50000
    `issued by the Authority` IS TRUE
    `withdrawn by Gazette notification` IS FALSE
    `impaired otherwise than by fair wear and tear` IS FALSE
    `defaced by a mark, writing or cutting` IS FALSE
    `damaged by an IBNS activation` IS FALSE
    `payee gave written notice refusing the denomination` IS FALSE

